---
/**
 * careers.astro — 招聘页
 *
 * 刻意不写：具体在招岗位、薪资区间、福利清单、人数增长 —— 这些我无从核实，
 * 编出来就是下一个「+86 123 4567 8900」。所以本页只做一件事：
 * 说清楚我们在哪、做什么类型的工作、以及怎么把简历递到人手上。
 * 真有岗位开放时，把岗位清单加进 roles 数组即可，页面结构不用动。
 */
import DocPage from "../layouts/DocPage.astro";
import { companyFacts } from "../lib/companyProfile";
---

<DocPage
    pageTitle="Careers"
    description="Work with MEIYU Aluminium in Dongguan — production, quality, engineering support and export sales roles. Send a speculative application."
    titleWhite="Work at"
    titleGold="MEIYU"
    eyebrow="Careers"
    subtitle="A Dongguan manufacturer of aluminium ceiling and facade systems."
>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
        {companyFacts.name} makes architectural aluminium products — ceiling tiles,
        linear and baffle ceilings, wall and facade panels, honeycomb and veneer panels
        — in our own plant in {companyFacts.location}, and ships them to
        building projects overseas.
    </p>
    <p>
        That combination shapes the kind of person the work suits: detail-minded
        about dimensions and finish, comfortable when the reference document is
        a setting-out drawing rather than a marketing brief, and patient with
        the questions an international specifier asks.
    </p>

    <h2>The kind of work here</h2>
    <p>
        Roles at the plant and the export office generally fall into four
        groups:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Production</strong> — roll forming, press brake and folding, perforation,
            coating line operation and packing.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Quality</strong> — incoming material checks against mill certificates,
            first-article sign-off, coating thickness and adhesion, final inspection
            before packing.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Engineering support</strong> — reading and preparing shop drawings,
            setting-out, and turning a concept into a product family that can actually
            be made.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Export sales and order follow-up</strong> — enquiries, quotations,
            sample approvals, and seeing an order through production to the container.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="doc-note">
        We do not keep a live job board on this website. If you are asking
        whether we have an opening right now, the honest answer is that it
        changes week to week — so send us your details and we will contact you
        when something fits.
    </div>

    <h2>How to apply</h2>
    <p>
        Email the following to <a href={`mailto:${companyFacts.email}`}
            >{companyFacts.email}</a
        >:
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li>
            The type of work you want to do (one of the four groups above is
            enough).
        </li>
        <li>Where you have done it before, and for how long.</li>
        <li>
            What you can start with — a machine, a drawing set, a coating line,
            a market.
        </li>
        <li>Your location and, if relevant, your availability.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
        A short, specific message tells us more than a formatted CV. If you have
        photographs of work you have made or drawings you have produced, attach
        them.
    </p>

    <p class="doc-updated">
        {companyFacts.location} · Applications to
        <a href={`mailto:${companyFacts.email}`}>{companyFacts.email}</a>
    </p>
</DocPage>
